.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WLAN 4
.Os Rach2
.Sh NAME
.Nm wlan
.Nd wireless station network interfaces
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A registered radio appears as
.Li phyN
with an Ethernet interface named
.Li wlanN .
The interface is initially down.
Bringing it up starts the radio; taking it down ends a scan, deauthenticates
from the access point and stops the radio.
While it is down, a scan, an authentication, an association or a management
frame asked for through
.Xr nl80211 7
fails with
.Er ENETDOWN .
It uses the ordinary IP, ARP, DHCP and packet-socket paths.
Association gives carrier; authorization opens the control port.
Before authorization only EAPOL, EtherType 0x888e, passes in either direction.
A stopped, blocked or unassociated radio passes no data.
Each radio has a switch of
.Xr rfkill 4 ,
.Li phyN ,
whose block leaves the network and stops the radio, and whose release starts
it again if it ran.
.Pp
The station converts Ethernet II frames to three-address 802.11 data frames
with LLC/SNAP headers.
IPX and AARP use the IEEE 802.1H bridge-tunnel header.
An 802.3 frame keeps its LLC payload, with Ethernet padding omitted.
The receive conversion accepts data and QoS data after decryption and
reassembly; it refuses four-address, null and aggregate frames.
.Pp
The world regulatory domain permits active use of channels 1 through 11,
passive use of 12 and 13, and no use of 14.
The radio's EEPROM capabilities can restrict this further.
An EEPROM country of US or CA disables channels 12 and 13.
Power is at most 20 dBm and never greater than the radio advertises.
.Pp
Wireless extensions are absent.
.Dv SIOCGIWNAME
returns
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /proc/net/wireless
Link quality from 0 to 70, signal and noise in signed dBm, discard counters
and missed beacons, in Linux's format.
.It Pa /sys/class/ieee80211/phyN
The radio's
.Pa index ,
.Pa name ,
.Pa macaddress
and
.Pa uevent
attributes.
.It Pa /sys/class/net/wlanN/phy80211
A link to the radio.
.It Pa /sys/class/net/wlanN/device/driver
A link whose final component is the registered radio driver name.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr rfkill 4 ,
.Xr wsim 4 ,
.Xr proc 5 ,
.Xr sysfs 5 ,
.Xr nl80211 7
